ocedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~exc_recursive~~CalledByGraph proc~exc_recursive exc_recursive proc~exc_recursive->proc~exc_recursive proc~get_exc_positive get_exc_positive proc~get_exc_positive->proc~exc_recursive proc~get_exc get_exc proc~get_exc->proc~get_exc_positive proc~compute_total_energy compute_total_energy proc~compute_total_energy->proc~get_exc proc~populate_xc_output_cache populate_xc_output_cache proc~populate_xc_output_cache->proc~get_exc Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code recursive function exc_recursive ( xc , n_up_in , n_dw_in ) result ( exc ) type ( xc_lsda_t ), intent ( in ) :: xc real ( dp ), intent ( in ) :: n_up_in , n_dw_in real ( dp ) :: exc integer :: region real ( dp ) :: n_up , n_dw , n_up_map , n_dw_map , n , m , n_up_c , n_dw_c ! Snap onto the region boundaries first, then use the snapped pair for ! the shortcuts, the region decision AND the evaluation (see ! `snap_to_boundaries`). call snap_to_boundaries ( n_up_in , n_dw_in , n_up , n_dw , n , m ) if ( is_corner_shortcut ( n , m )) then exc = 0.0_dp return end if ! Empty spin-down (|n - m| < tol) or empty spin-up (|n + m| < tol) if ( abs ( n - m ) < EMPTY_CHANNEL_TOL . or . abs ( n + m ) < EMPTY_CHANNEL_TOL ) then exc = 0.0_dp return end if region = determine_region ( n , m ) if ( region /= 1 ) then ! Regions II, III and IV: recurse on the transformed pair, exactly as ! the C++ does. e_xc is invariant (no sign flip, no spin exchange). call apply_symmetry_transform ( region , n_up , n_dw , n_up_map , n_dw_map ) exc = exc_recursive ( xc , n_up_map , n_dw_map ) return end if ! Region I: clip to the tabulated range to absorb roundoff at the ! boundaries (the particle-hole transform can produce -1e-17) n_up_c = max ( 0.0_dp , min ( 1.0_dp , n_up )) n_dw_c = max ( 0.0_dp , min ( 1.0_dp , n_dw )) call convert_to_nm ( n_up_c , n_dw_c , n , m ) ! Fully polarized beyond the last tabulated density: e_xc = 0. ! Literal guard of the C++ `exc_value`; it also keeps the density ! spline below from degenerating to a zero-width window. if ( m > xc % spl_exc % x ( xc % spl_exc % n_x ) - 1.0e-15_dp ) then exc = 0.0_dp return end if ! Evaluate spline. The synthetic node at n = m is the fully polarized ! line, where e_xc vanishes; the prescribed derivative there is ! (∂e_xc/∂n_dn)/2 = (de_xc/dn) at fixed magnetization. exc = spline2d_eval ( xc % spl_exc , n , m , & node0_value = 0.0_dp , & dfdx_first = 0.5_dp * dexc_dndown_b0 ( abs ( xc % U ), m )) end function exc_recursive","tags":"","url":"proc/exc_recursive.html"},{"title":"is_corner_shortcut – LSDA-Hubbard-Fortran","text":"private  function is_corner_shortcut(n, m) result(hit) Fully polarized corner shortcut of the C++ reference Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: n real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: m Return Value logical Called by proc~~is_corner_shortcut~~CalledByGraph proc~is_corner_shortcut is_corner_shortcut proc~exc_recursive exc_recursive proc~exc_recursive->proc~is_corner_shortcut proc~exc_recursive->proc~exc_recursive proc~vxc_dn_recursive vxc_dn_recursive proc~vxc_dn_recu